{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ta9yXbMc589Gabp4agBMub","type":"tool_result","content":"   100→  @spec init({listener_id :: neg_integer(), server_pid :: pid(), Abyss.ServerConfig.t()}) ::\n   101→          {:ok, state} | {:stop, term}\n   102→  def init({listener_id, server_pid, server_config}) do\n   103→    broadcast = server_config.broadcast\n   104→\n   105→    transport_options =\n   106→      if broadcast do\n   107→        server_config.transport_options\n   108→        |> Keyword.put(:active, true)\n   109→        |> Keyword.put(:broadcast, true)\n   110→        |> Keyword.put(:recbuf, server_config.udp_buffer_size)\n   111→        |> Keyword.put(:sndbuf, server_config.udp_buffer_size)\n   112→      else\n   113→        server_config.transport_options\n   114→        |> Keyword.put(:active, false)\n   115→        |> Keyword.put(:broadcast, false)\n   116→        |> Keyword.put(:recbuf, server_config.udp_buffer_size)\n   117→        |> Keyword.put(:sndbuf, server_config.udp_buffer_size)\n   118→      end\n   119→\n   120→    transport = server_config.transport_module\n   121→\n   122→    with {:ok, listener_socket} <-\n   123→           transport.listen(\n   124→             server_config.port,\n   125→             transport_options\n   126→           ),\n   127→         {:ok, {ip, port}} <-\n   128→           :inet.sockname(listener_socket) do\n   129→      active =\n   130→        case transport.getopts(listener_socket, [:active]) do\n   131→          {:ok, [active: true]} -> true\n   132→          _ -> false\n   133→        end\n   134→\n   135→      span_metadata = %{\n   136→        listener_id: listener_id,\n   137→        listener_socket: listener_socket,\n   138→        handler: server_config.handler_module,\n   139→        local_address: ip,\n   140→        local_port: port,\n   141→        broadcast: broadcast,\n   142→        transport_options: transport_options\n   143→      }\n   144→\n   145→      listener_span = Abyss.Telemetry.start_span(:listener, %{}, span_metadata)\n   146→\n   147→      state = %{\n   148→        broadcast: broadcast,\n   149→        is_active: active,\n   150→        is_listening: false,\n   151→        server_config: server_config,\n   152→        server_pid: server_pid,\n   153→        listener_id: listener_id,\n   154→        listener_socket: listener_socket,\n   155→        listener_span: listener_span,\n   156→        local_info: {ip, port},\n   157→        transport: transport\n   158→      }\n   159→\n   160→      # Start listening immediately for non-broadcast mode\n   161→      if not broadcast do\n   162→        Process.send_after(self(), :start_listening, 0)\n   163→      end\n   164→\n   165→      {:ok, state}\n   166→    else\n   167→      {:error, reason} ->\n   168→        {:stop, reason}\n   169→    end\n   170→  end\n   171→\n   172→  @impl GenServer\n   173→  def handle_info(\n   174→        :start_listening,\n   175→        %{listener_socket: listener_socket, transport: transport} = state\n   176→      ) do\n   177→    if state.is_listening do\n   178→      {:noreply, state}\n   179→    else\n   180→      case transport.getopts(listener_socket, [:active]) do\n   181→        {:ok, [{:active, false}]} ->\n   182→          Abyss.Telemetry.span_event(state.listener_span, :ready, %{}, %{\n   183→            listener_id: state.listener_id,\n   184→            listener_socket: state.listener_socket,\n   185→            local_info: state.local_info\n   186→          })\n   187→\n   188→          Process.send_after(self(), :do_recv, 0)\n   189→          {:noreply, state |> Map.put(:is_listening, true)}\n   190→\n   191→        {:ok, [active: true]} ->\n   192→          {:noreply, state}\n   193→      end\n   194→    end\n   195→  end\n   196→\n   197→  def handle_info({:udp, socket, ip, port, data}, %{listener_span: listener_span} = state) do\n   198→    # Check packet size\n   199→    if byte_size(data) > state.server_config.max_packet_size do\n   200→      Abyss.Telemetry.span_event(listener_span, :packet_too_large, %{\n   201→        remote_address: ip,\n   202→        remote_port: port,\n   203→        packet_size: byte_size(data),\n   204→        max_size: state.server_config.max_packet_size\n   205→      })\n   206→\n   207→      {:noreply, state}\n   208→    else\n   209→      start_time = Abyss.Telemetry.monotonic_time()\n   210→\n   211→      # Track connection acceptance\n   212→      Abyss.Telemetry.track_connection_accepted()\n   213→\n   214→      connection_span =\n   215→        Abyss.Telemetry.start_child_span_with_sampling(\n   216→          listener_span,\n   217→          :connection,\n   218→          %{monotonic_time: start_time},\n   219→          %{remote_address: ip, remote_port: port, accept_start_time: start_time},\n   220→          sample_rate: state.server_config.connection_telemetry_sample_rate\n   221→        )\n   222→\n   223→      Abyss.Connection.start_active(\n   224→        state.server_pid,\n   225→        self(),\n   226→        socket,\n   227→        {ip, port, data},\n   228→        state.server_config,\n   229→        connection_span\n   230→      )\n   231→\n   232→      {:noreply, state}\n   233→    end\n   234→  end\n   235→\n   236→  def handle_info(\n   237→        :do_recv,\n   238→        %{listener_span: listener_span, listener_socket: listener_socket, transport: transport} =\n   239→          state\n   240→      ) do\n   241→    Abyss.Telemetry.untimed_span_event(state.listener_span, :waiting, %{}, %{\n   242→      listener_id: state.listener_id,\n   243→      listener_socket: state.listener_socket,\n   244→      local_info: state.local_info\n   245→    })\n   246→\n   247→    case transport.recv(listener_socket, 0, :infinity) do\n   248→      {:ok, {ip, port, data}} ->\n   249→        Abyss.Telemetry.untimed_span_event(state.listener_span, :receiving, %{}, %{\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50d21925-9237-40c9-8dd2-03e5c6e35c37","uuid":"0592349c-52db-4646-beb4-1a9683a307cd","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/abyss/lib/abyss/listener.ex","content":"  @spec init({listener_id :: neg_integer(), server_pid :: pid(), Abyss.ServerConfig.t()}) ::\n          {:ok, state} | {:stop, term}\n  def init({listener_id, server_pid, server_config}) do\n    broadcast = server_config.broadcast\n\n    transport_options =\n      if broadcast do\n        server_config.transport_options\n        |> Keyword.put(:active, true)\n        |> Keyword.put(:broadcast, true)\n        |> Keyword.put(:recbuf, server_config.udp_buffer_size)\n        |> Keyword.put(:sndbuf, server_config.udp_buffer_size)\n      else\n        server_config.transport_options\n        |> Keyword.put(:active, false)\n        |> Keyword.put(:broadcast, false)\n        |> Keyword.put(:recbuf, server_config.udp_buffer_size)\n        |> Keyword.put(:sndbuf, server_config.udp_buffer_size)\n      end\n\n    transport = server_config.transport_module\n\n    with {:ok, listener_socket} <-\n           transport.listen(\n             server_config.port,\n             transport_options\n           ),\n         {:ok, {ip, port}} <-\n           :inet.sockname(listener_socket) do\n      active =\n        case transport.getopts(listener_socket, [:active]) do\n          {:ok, [active: true]} -> true\n          _ -> false\n        end\n\n      span_metadata = %{\n        listener_id: listener_id,\n        listener_socket: listener_socket,\n        handler: server_config.handler_module,\n        local_address: ip,\n        local_port: port,\n        broadcast: broadcast,\n        transport_options: transport_options\n      }\n\n      listener_span = Abyss.Telemetry.start_span(:listener, %{}, span_metadata)\n\n      state = %{\n        broadcast: broadcast,\n        is_active: active,\n        is_listening: false,\n        server_config: server_config,\n        server_pid: server_pid,\n        listener_id: listener_id,\n        listener_socket: listener_socket,\n        listener_span: listener_span,\n        local_info: {ip, port},\n        transport: transport\n      }\n\n      # Start listening immediately for non-broadcast mode\n      if not broadcast do\n        Process.send_after(self(), :start_listening, 0)\n      end\n\n      {:ok, state}\n    else\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        {:stop, reason}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl GenServer\n  def handle_info(\n        :start_listening,\n        %{listener_socket: listener_socket, transport: transport} = state\n      ) do\n    if state.is_listening do\n      {:noreply, state}\n    else\n      case transport.getopts(listener_socket, [:active]) do\n        {:ok, [{:active, false}]} ->\n          Abyss.Telemetry.span_event(state.listener_span, :ready, %{}, %{\n            listener_id: state.listener_id,\n            listener_socket: state.listener_socket,\n            local_info: state.local_info\n          })\n\n          Process.send_after(self(), :do_recv, 0)\n          {:noreply, state |> Map.put(:is_listening, true)}\n\n        {:ok, [active: true]} ->\n          {:noreply, state}\n      end\n    end\n  end\n\n  def handle_info({:udp, socket, ip, port, data}, %{listener_span: listener_span} = state) do\n    # Check packet size\n    if byte_size(data) > state.server_config.max_packet_size do\n      Abyss.Telemetry.span_event(listener_span, :packet_too_large, %{\n        remote_address: ip,\n        remote_port: port,\n        packet_size: byte_size(data),\n        max_size: state.server_config.max_packet_size\n      })\n\n      {:noreply, state}\n    else\n      start_time = Abyss.Telemetry.monotonic_time()\n\n      # Track connection acceptance\n      Abyss.Telemetry.track_connection_accepted()\n\n      connection_span =\n        Abyss.Telemetry.start_child_span_with_sampling(\n          listener_span,\n          :connection,\n          %{monotonic_time: start_time},\n          %{remote_address: ip, remote_port: port, accept_start_time: start_time},\n          sample_rate: state.server_config.connection_telemetry_sample_rate\n        )\n\n      Abyss.Connection.start_active(\n        state.server_pid,\n        self(),\n        socket,\n        {ip, port, data},\n        state.server_config,\n        connection_span\n      )\n\n      {:noreply, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  def handle_info(\n        :do_recv,\n        %{listener_span: listener_span, listener_socket: listener_socket, transport: transport} =\n          state\n      ) do\n    Abyss.Telemetry.untimed_span_event(state.listener_span, :waiting, %{}, %{\n      listener_id: state.listener_id,\n      listener_socket: state.listener_socket,\n      local_info: state.local_info\n    })\n\n    case transport.recv(listener_socket, 0, :infinity) do\n      {:ok, {ip, port, data}} ->\n        Abyss.Telemetry.untimed_span_event(state.listener_span, :receiving, %{}, %{","numLines":150,"startLine":100,"totalLines":446}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01C61VMdkQAdUL5SRVWcX1oW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\n**Root Cause Found**: At line 247, `transport.recv(listener_socket, 0, :infinity)` is a **blocking call with infinite timeout**. When a GenServer is blocked in `handle_info` doing a synchronous receive, it cannot respond to `handle_call` messages. This is why `listener_info/1` times out.\n\n**Solution Options**:\n1. Use `active: true` socket mode (currently only used for broadcast)\n2. Change the recv timeout from `:infinity` to a finite value with retry\n3. Store listener info during init before blocking recv starts\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nThe real issue is the test helper is trying to get the port from a blocking listener. Let me examine how the test works - the port info is stored in `state.local_info` during init, so we should be able to get it before the listener starts blocking.\n\nLooking back at the code:\n- Line 128: `{:ok, {ip, port}} <- :inet.sockname(listener_socket)` - port is determined\n- Line 156: `local_info: {ip, port}` - stored in state\n- Line 162: `Process.send_after(self(), :start_listening, 0)` - starts listening asynchronously\n\nThe problem is that `start_listening` triggers `:do_recv` which blocks the GenServer. The test tries to get port info AFTER the server is already blocking.\n\nHowever, the real solution is that E2E tests run but DNS E2E tests fail more frequently due to the blocking nature. Let me look at a simpler solution - the E2E tests with mDNS, DHCPv4, and DHCPv6 pass. The DNS tests fail specifically because the DNS server uses Abyss in a non-broadcast mode which blocks.\n\nLet me check if the DNS tests run in separate process isolation:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2090,"cache_read_input_tokens":114134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2090,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50d21925-9237-40c9-8dd2-03e5c6e35c37","uuid":"7006ff1d-7c98-4ffa-adab-c9ed9625c7ac"}
