{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01D3fFeRKzQo21qSM9cb1EYe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The best solution is to use `active: once` or `active: true` mode instead of blocking `recv`. But modifying Abyss deeply is risky. A simpler workaround is to modify the DNS E2E test helper to use the DNS server's already-existing `get_udp_port` function before the listener starts blocking.\n\nActually, looking at the code more carefully:\n- Line 162: `Process.send_after(self(), :start_listening, 0)` - async, should allow `handle_call` before this triggers\n- Line 188: `Process.send_after(self(), :do_recv, 0)` - also async\n\nThe problem is that by the time the test calls `get_udp_port`, the listener has already entered the blocking `recv` call. The solution is to use active mode for the DNS server as well.\n\nLet me look at a simpler fix - modifying the Abyss listener to use a reasonable timeout with retry instead of blocking forever:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1062,"cache_read_input_tokens":119393,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1062,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50d21925-9237-40c9-8dd2-03e5c6e35c37","uuid":"d3536ef9-439a-4790-ab50-07ca3d54a76a"}
