{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VGpSauhUNBrvKHhAwvKr42","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  IP address pool management for DHCPv4.\n     4→\n     5→  Manages IP address ranges, allocation, and availability tracking.\n     6→  Supports multiple pools, static reservations, and address conflict detection.\n     7→  \"\"\"\n     8→\n     9→  @type ip_address :: {0..255, 0..255, 0..255, 0..255}\n    10→  @type mac_address :: binary()\n    11→  @type ip_range :: {ip_address(), ip_address()}\n    12→  @type pool_config :: %{\n    13→          name: String.t(),\n    14→          ranges: [ip_range()],\n    15→          # Legacy support - converted to ranges\n    16→          range_start: ip_address() | nil,\n    17→          range_end: ip_address() | nil,\n    18→          excluded_ranges: [ip_range()],\n    19→          subnet_mask: ip_address(),\n    20→          gateway: ip_address(),\n    21→          dns_servers: [ip_address()],\n    22→          domain_name: String.t() | nil,\n    23→          lease_time: pos_integer()\n    24→        }\n    25→\n    26→  @doc \"\"\"\n    27→  Creates a new address pool from configuration.\n    28→\n    29→  ## Parameters\n    30→  - `config` - Pool configuration map\n    31→\n    32→  ## Returns\n    33→  - `{:ok, pool}` - Successfully created pool\n    34→  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to create pool\n    35→\n    36→  ## Example\n    37→      iex> config = %{\n    38→      ...>   name: \"main\",\n    39→      ...>   range_start: {192, 168, 1, 100},\n    40→      ...>   range_end: {192, 168, 1, 200},\n    41→      ...>   subnet_mask: {255, 255, 255, 0},\n    42→      ...>   gateway: {192, 168, 1, 1},\n    43→      ...>   dns_servers: [{192, 168, 1, 1}],\n    44→      ...>   domain_name: \"local\",\n    45→      ...>   lease_time: 86400\n    46→      ...> }\n    47→      iex> YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool.new(config)\n    48→      {:ok, %{...}}\n    49→  \"\"\"\n    50→  @spec new(map()) :: {:ok, pool_config()} | {:error, term()}\n    51→  def new(config) do\n    52→    with {:ok, validated_config} <- validate_pool_config(config) do\n    53→      # Support both legacy (range_start/range_end) and new (ranges) format\n    54→      ranges = build_ranges(config, validated_config)\n    55→      excluded_ranges = build_excluded_ranges(config)\n    56→\n    57→      # Get first range for defaults\n    58→      {first_range_start, _} = hd(ranges)\n    59→\n    60→      pool = %{\n    61→        name: Map.get(config, :name, \"default\"),\n    62→        ranges: ranges,\n    63→        range_start: validated_config[:range_start],\n    64→        range_end: validated_config[:range_end],\n    65→        excluded_ranges: excluded_ranges,\n    66→        subnet_mask: Map.get(config, :subnet_mask, {255, 255, 255, 0}),\n    67→        gateway: Map.get(config, :gateway, first_range_start),\n    68→        dns_servers: Map.get(config, :dns_servers, [first_range_start]),\n    69→        domain_name: Map.get(config, :domain_name),\n    70→        lease_time: Map.get(config, :lease_time, 86400),\n    71→        static_reservations: Map.get(config, :static_reservations, %{})\n    72→      }\n    73→\n    74→      {:ok, pool}\n    75→    end\n    76→  end\n    77→\n    78→  @doc \"\"\"\n    79→  Validates pool configuration.\n    80→\n    81→  Supports both legacy format (range_start/range_end) and new format (ranges).\n    82→\n    83→  ## Parameters\n    84→  - `config` - Pool configuration to validate\n    85→\n    86→  ## Returns\n    87→  - `{:ok, config}` - Valid configuration\n    88→  - `{:error, reason}` - Invalid configuration\n    89→  \"\"\"\n    90→  @spec validate_pool_config(map()) :: {:ok, map()} | {:error, term()}\n    91→  def validate_pool_config(config) do\n    92→    cond do\n    93→      # New format with ranges\n    94→      Map.has_key?(config, :ranges) && is_list(config.ranges) ->\n    95→        validate_ranges_config(config)\n    96→\n    97→      # Legacy format with range_start/range_end\n    98→      Map.has_key?(config, :range_start) || Map.has_key?(config, \"range_start\") ->\n    99→        validate_legacy_config(config)\n   100→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GysfH7RjSXXrDh7G4bTCfc","session_id":"50d21925-9237-40c9-8dd2-03e5c6e35c37","uuid":"395b165c-9620-40b9-a195-c5a74b1f85b6","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/address_pool.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  IP address pool management for DHCPv4.\n\n  Manages IP address ranges, allocation, and availability tracking.\n  Supports multiple pools, static reservations, and address conflict detection.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  @type ip_address :: {0..255, 0..255, 0..255, 0..255}\n  @type mac_address :: binary()\n  @type ip_range :: {ip_address(), ip_address()}\n  @type pool_config :: %{\n          name: String.t(),\n          ranges: [ip_range()],\n          # Legacy support - converted to ranges\n          range_start: ip_address() | nil,\n          range_end: ip_address() | nil,\n          excluded_ranges: [ip_range()],\n          subnet_mask: ip_address(),\n          gateway: ip_address(),\n          dns_servers: [ip_address()],\n          domain_name: String.t() | nil,\n          lease_time: pos_integer()\n        }\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Creates a new address pool from configuration.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `config` - Pool configuration map\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, pool}` - Successfully created pool\n  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to create pool\n\n  ## Example\n      iex> config = %{\n      ...>   name: \"main\",\n      ...>   range_start: {192, 168, 1, 100},\n      ...>   range_end: {192, 168, 1, 200},\n      ...>   subnet_mask: {255, 255, 255, 0},\n      ...>   gateway: {192, 168, 1, 1},\n      ...>   dns_servers: [{192, 168, 1, 1}],\n      ...>   domain_name: \"local\",\n      ...>   lease_time: 86400\n      ...> }\n      iex> YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool.new(config)\n      {:ok, %{...}}\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec new(map()) :: {:ok, pool_config()} | {:error, term()}\n  def new(config) do\n    with {:ok, validated_config} <- validate_pool_config(config) do\n      # Support both legacy (range_start/range_end) and new (ranges) format\n      ranges = build_ranges(config, validated_config)\n      excluded_ranges = build_excluded_ranges(config)\n\n      # Get first range for defaults\n      {first_range_start, _} = hd(ranges)\n\n      pool = %{\n        name: Map.get(config, :name, \"default\"),\n        ranges: ranges,\n        range_start: validated_config[:range_start],\n        range_end: validated_config[:range_end],\n        excluded_ranges: excluded_ranges,\n        subnet_mask: Map.get(config, :subnet_mask, {255, 255, 255, 0}),\n        gateway: Map.get(config, :gateway, first_range_start),\n        dns_servers: Map.get(config, :dns_servers, [first_range_start]),\n        domain_name: Map.get(config, :domain_name),\n        lease_time: Map.get(config, :lease_time, 86400),\n        static_reservations: Map.get(config, :static_reservations, %{})\n      }\n\n      {:ok, pool}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Validates pool configuration.\n\n  Supports both legacy format (range_start/range_end) and new format (ranges).\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `config` - Pool configuration to validate\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, config}` - Valid configuration\n  - `{:error, reason}` - Invalid configuration\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec validate_pool_config(map()) :: {:ok, map()} | {:error, term()}\n  def validate_pool_config(config) do\n    cond do\n      # New format with ranges\n      Map.has_key?(config, :ranges) && is_list(config.ranges) ->\n        validate_ranges_config(config)\n\n      # Legacy format with range_start/range_end\n      Map.has_key?(config, :range_start) || Map.has_key?(config, \"range_start\") ->\n        validate_legacy_config(config)\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":412}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019LWGzCSMCtj1BvhdpVNrZ4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Mdns.ServiceRegistry do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Registry for managing locally registered mDNS services.\n     4→\n     5→  Stores service definitions in ETS for fast lookups, manages service lifecycle\n     6→  (probing, announcing, registered), and handles persistence to/from files.\n     7→  \"\"\"\n     8→\n     9→  use GenServer\n    10→\n    11→  alias YellowDog.Mdns.ServiceStore\n    12→\n    13→  @table_name :mdns_service_registry\n    14→  @ets_options [:named_table, :public, :set, read_concurrency: true, write_concurrency: true]\n    15→\n    16→  @type service_id :: String.t()\n    17→  @type service_state :: :probing | :announcing | :registered | :disabled\n    18→\n    19→  @type service :: %{\n    20→          id: service_id(),\n    21→          name: String.t(),\n    22→          type: String.t(),\n    23→          domain: String.t(),\n    24→          fqdn: String.t(),\n    25→          host: String.t(),\n    26→          port: pos_integer(),\n    27→          txt_records: map(),\n    28→          addresses: [tuple()],\n    29→          priority: non_neg_integer(),\n    30→          weight: non_neg_integer(),\n    31→          ttl: pos_integer(),\n    32→          state: service_state(),\n    33→          source: :file | :api,\n    34→          enabled: boolean(),\n    35→          registered_at: integer(),\n    36→          last_announced: integer() | nil\n    37→        }\n    38→\n    39→  # Default TTLs per RFC 6762\n    40→  @default_service_ttl 4500\n    41→  # 75 minutes\n    42→\n    43→  # Client API\n    44→\n    45→  @doc \"\"\"\n    46→  Starts the ServiceRegistry GenServer.\n    47→  \"\"\"\n    48→  @spec start_link(keyword()) :: GenServer.on_start()\n    49→  def start_link(opts \\\\ []) do\n    50→    GenServer.start_link(__MODULE__, opts, name: __MODULE__)\n    51→  end\n    52→\n    53→  @doc \"\"\"\n    54→  Registers a new service.\n    55→\n    56→  ## Parameters\n    57→  - `service_def` - Service definition map\n    58→  - `opts` - Options\n    59→    - `:persist` - Save to file (default: false)\n    60→    - `:source` - Source of registration (:file or :api, default: :api)\n    61→\n    62→  ## Returns\n    63→  - `{:ok, service_id}` on success\n    64→  - `{:error, reason}` on failure\n    65→\n    66→  ## Examples\n    67→      iex> YellowDog.Mdns.ServiceRegistry.register_service(%{\n    68→      ...>   name: \"Web Server\",\n    69→      ...>   type: \"_http._tcp\",\n    70→      ...>   port: 8080,\n    71→      ...>   txt: %{\"path\" => \"/api\"}\n    72→      ...> })\n    73→      {:ok, \"Web Server._http._tcp.local\"}\n    74→  \"\"\"\n    75→  @spec register_service(map(), keyword()) :: {:ok, service_id()} | {:error, term()}\n    76→  def register_service(service_def, opts \\\\ []) do\n    77→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:register_service, service_def, opts})\n    78→  end\n    79→\n    80→  @doc \"\"\"\n    81→  Unregisters a service.\n    82→\n    83→  ## Parameters\n    84→  - `service_id` - Service identifier\n    85→  - `opts` - Options\n    86→    - `:persist` - Update file (default: false)\n    87→  \"\"\"\n    88→  @spec unregister_service(service_id(), keyword()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n    89→  def unregister_service(service_id, opts \\\\ []) do\n    90→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:unregister_service, service_id, opts})\n    91→  end\n    92→\n    93→  @doc \"\"\"\n    94→  Updates a service.\n    95→\n    96→  ## Parameters\n    97→  - `service_id` - Service identifier\n    98→  - `updates` - Map of fields to update\n    99→  - `opts` - Options\n   100→    - `:persist` - Save to file (default: false)\n   101→  \"\"\"\n   102→  @spec update_service(service_id(), map(), keyword()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n   103→  def update_service(service_id, updates, opts \\\\ []) do\n   104→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:update_service, service_id, updates, opts})\n   105→  end\n   106→\n   107→  @doc \"\"\"\n   108→  Enables or disables a service.\n   109→  \"\"\"\n   110→  @spec toggle_service(service_id()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n   111→  def toggle_service(service_id) do\n   112→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:toggle_service, service_id})\n   113→  end\n   114→\n   115→  @doc \"\"\"\n   116→  Gets a service by ID.\n   117→  \"\"\"\n   118→  @spec get_service(service_id()) :: service() | nil\n   119→  def get_service(service_id) do\n   120→    case :ets.lookup(@table_name, service_id) do\n   121→      [{^service_id, service}] -> service\n   122→      [] -> nil\n   123→    end\n   124→  end\n   125→\n   126→  @doc \"\"\"\n   127→  Lists all registered services.\n   128→\n   129→  ## Options\n   130→  - `:filter` - Filter services (:all, :enabled, :disabled, :registered)\n   131→  - `:source` - Filter by source (:file, :api, :all)\n   132→  \"\"\"\n   133→  @spec list_services(keyword()) :: [service()]\n   134→  def list_services(opts \\\\ []) do\n   135→    filter = Keyword.get(opts, :filter, :all)\n   136→    source_filter = Keyword.get(opts, :source, :all)\n   137→\n   138→    @table_name\n   139→    |> :ets.tab2list()\n   140→    |> Enum.map(fn {_id, service} -> service end)\n   141→    |> apply_filters(filter, source_filter)\n   142→    |> Enum.sort_by(& &1.name)\n   143→  end\n   144→\n   145→  @doc \"\"\"\n   146→  Gets DNS records for a query.\n   147→\n   148→  Used by the Responder to match incoming queries against registered services.\n   149→\n   150→  ## Parameters\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GysfH7RjSXXrDh7G4bTCfc","session_id":"50d21925-9237-40c9-8dd2-03e5c6e35c37","uuid":"ac443b9a-9200-44cc-9642-0aa104fd8ad1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/service_registry.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Mdns.ServiceRegistry do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Registry for managing locally registered mDNS services.\n\n  Stores service definitions in ETS for fast lookups, manages service lifecycle\n  (probing, announcing, registered), and handles persistence to/from files.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use GenServer\n\n  alias YellowDog.Mdns.ServiceStore\n\n  @table_name :mdns_service_registry\n  @ets_options [:named_table, :public, :set, read_concurrency: true, write_concurrency: true]\n\n  @type service_id :: String.t()\n  @type service_state :: :probing | :announcing | :registered | :disabled\n\n  @type service :: %{\n          id: service_id(),\n          name: String.t(),\n          type: String.t(),\n          domain: String.t(),\n          fqdn: String.t(),\n          host: String.t(),\n          port: pos_integer(),\n          txt_records: map(),\n          addresses: [tuple()],\n          priority: non_neg_integer(),\n          weight: non_neg_integer(),\n          ttl: pos_integer(),\n          state: service_state(),\n          source: :file | :api,\n          enabled: boolean(),\n          registered_at: integer(),\n          last_announced: integer() | nil\n        }\n\n  # Default TTLs per RFC 6762\n  @default_service_ttl 4500\n  # 75 minutes\n\n  # Client API\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Starts the ServiceRegistry GenServer.\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec start_link(keyword()) :: GenServer.on_start()\n  def start_link(opts \\\\ []) do\n    GenServer.start_link(__MODULE__, opts, name: __MODULE__)\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Registers a new service.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `service_def` - Service definition map\n  - `opts` - Options\n    - `:persist` - Save to file (default: false)\n    - `:source` - Source of registration (:file or :api, default: :api)\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, service_id}` on success\n  - `{:error, reason}` on failure\n\n  ## Examples\n      iex> YellowDog.Mdns.ServiceRegistry.register_service(%{\n      ...>   name: \"Web Server\",\n      ...>   type: \"_http._tcp\",\n      ...>   port: 8080,\n      ...>   txt: %{\"path\" => \"/api\"}\n      ...> })\n      {:ok, \"Web Server._http._tcp.local\"}\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec register_service(map(), keyword()) :: {:ok, service_id()} | {:error, term()}\n  def register_service(service_def, opts \\\\ []) do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:register_service, service_def, opts})\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Unregisters a service.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `service_id` - Service identifier\n  - `opts` - Options\n    - `:persist` - Update file (default: false)\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec unregister_service(service_id(), keyword()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n  def unregister_service(service_id, opts \\\\ []) do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:unregister_service, service_id, opts})\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Updates a service.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `service_id` - Service identifier\n  - `updates` - Map of fields to update\n  - `opts` - Options\n    - `:persist` - Save to file (default: false)\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec update_service(service_id(), map(), keyword()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n  def update_service(service_id, updates, opts \\\\ []) do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:update_service, service_id, updates, opts})\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Enables or disables a service.\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec toggle_service(service_id()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n  def toggle_service(service_id) do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:toggle_service, service_id})\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets a service by ID.\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec get_service(service_id()) :: service() | nil\n  def get_service(service_id) do\n    case :ets.lookup(@table_name, service_id) do\n      [{^service_id, service}] -> service\n      [] -> nil\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Lists all registered services.\n\n  ## Options\n  - `:filter` - Filter services (:all, :enabled, :disabled, :registered)\n  - `:source` - Filter by source (:file, :api, :all)\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec list_services(keyword()) :: [service()]\n  def list_services(opts \\\\ []) do\n    filter = Keyword.get(opts, :filter, :all)\n    source_filter = Keyword.get(opts, :source, :all)\n\n    @table_name\n    |> :ets.tab2list()\n    |> Enum.map(fn {_id, service} -> service end)\n    |> apply_filters(filter, source_filter)\n    |> Enum.sort_by(& &1.name)\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets DNS records for a query.\n\n  Used by the Responder to match incoming queries against registered services.\n\n  ## Parameters","numLines":150,"startLine":1,"totalLines":571}}}
